[/kaggle/repo/disaster-tweets-bert-0-835score.ipynb:cell 15] — The `WeightedLossTrainer` class overrides `get_eval_dataloader`:
```python
class WeightedLossTrainer(Trainer):
    def get_eval_dataloader(self, eval_dataset=None):
        eval_dataset = eval_dataset if eval_dataset is not None else self.eval_dataset
        return DataLoader(eval_dataset, batch_size=self.args.per_device_eval_batch_size, shuffle=True, collate_fn=self.data_collator)
```
This explicitly passes `shuffle=True` to the DataLoader used for validation/evaluation. The `Trainer` calls `get_eval_dataloader` when running `trainer.evaluate()` (also called in the notebook), confirming this shuffles validation data during evaluation.
